<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n104038" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίνῠμαι</span></b> , inf.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίνυσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Op.</u>
					711
				</span></i>
			:—poet. for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίνομαι</span>
			(v. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίνω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11
				</span></i>
			), <i>punish, chastise</i>, c. acc. pers., [
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ζεὺς] τίνυται ὅς τις ἁμάρτῃ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					13.214
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἳ . . ἀνθρώπους τίνυσθον, ὅτις κ᾽
					ἐπίορκον ὀμόσσῃ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					3.279
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				19.260
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Crass.</u>
				21
			</span></i>: c. acc. rei, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λώβην τινύμενος</span>
			<i>chastising</i> insolence, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				24.326
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>avenge, take vengeance for</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὅρκον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Op.</u>
					804
				</span></i>
			 (v.l.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἵματος δίκαν,
			φόνον</span>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Or.</u>
				323
			</span></i> (lyr.): abs., <i>avenge oneself</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				5.77
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>repay</i>, of the punisher, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δὶς τόσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Op.</u>
					711
				</span></i>
			; of the punished, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔνδικα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					11.374
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Maced.
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>repay</i>, in good sense, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. κομιδὴν
				παιδοτροφίης</span> Opp <i><span class="en">
				<u>C.</u>
				2.349
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Act.
			, <i>pay</i> penalty, only in late writers, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δίκας</span></div>
